Z||000005||82-T/A||12-03-2000||09:17 AM||||I tend to agree, they look like they came off the back of a big Chevy pickup. Those are pickup truck exhaust pipes.<P>IMHO, the BEST exhaust pipes for the aero nosed Fieros, are the stock exhaust pipes.<P>IMHO, the best exhaust pipes for the Coupe Fieros (2m4, 2m6, Formula) are the Ocelot Chrome plated Fiero tips.<P><P>------------------<BR>Todd Jaspers<BR>1997 Pontiac GrandAm SE<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero SE/V6<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2m4 SE<BR>http://www.ezshots.com/album.cgi?82tafiero/Apartment||||reg||1
Z||000006||2xsess||12-03-2000||11:39 AM||||Sorry but I agree with the general opinion here, when I lived in FL I saw those on almost every pickup and mustang and camaro on the road. <P>I think they look too big on the Fiero and a little ricey.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||DaRkLoRD||12-03-2000||12:08 PM||||IMHO, they're a bit too big for a 2.8... if you had say.. a big block V8, then they might be appropriate.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I'm going with quad chrome 2.5" tips.. I think it'll look better than the stock tips, without being too large or obvious.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||jlhuber||12-03-2000||01:32 PM||||I looked at another view of the car (car is not mine for those who may not know) and it looks they stick out about 6-8 inches beyond the rear fascia.   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1359159&a=10128384&p=34633048">   That is a bit too far for my taste also.  I agree about the truck/mustang thing to a certain degree, the pipes do need to be connected to a bigger motor than stock... I'm thinking the good ole 350.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I thank you for your opinions on this.  I am looking at my options once again (3800SII/350/3.2turbo) for when I get my next fiero, and I am also looking for some pipes that will fit the body design and motor.  They can stick out little further than the stock GT pipes.  I am looking for something that will give me a single pipe on each side instead of the dual twins, not be too big, or stick out too far.  Any ideas/pics?<P>thanx<P>--jess<BR><p>[This message has been edited by jlhuber (edited 12-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||12-03-2000||02:42 PM||||Last time I was home, I went to Canadian Tire and was checking out some stuff in the exhaust section.. I found some tips that were 2.5" inner diameter, but 3.25" outer diameter. They looked pretty cool. a bit big for my tastes, but they give the impression of being a bigger tip than it actually is..<P>I think having 1 of those in each of the exhaust cutouts would look kinda nice actually. it was big enough to seem agressive, but not so much that it'd be ricey.<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 12-03-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000010||sqoach||12-03-2000||03:00 PM||||hmmm...i agree with most of the guys.  lots of people around here have chevy shortbed's with pipes just like that.  there's also a few camaros and firebirds.  too big for me.  lol...imagine having twin tips that size  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh<BR>fiero7@hotmail.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig.JPG"> ||||reg||11
Z||000011||Patrick's Dad||12-03-2000||07:42 PM||||That's too much....<P>Too much for me, visually. IMO, it's rice.<P>From what I've learned about exhaust, it's also too much, as in, too big. That much pipe volume means that that airflow in the pipes doesn't move very fast, creating (or not creating...) enough vacuum to remove the exhaust charge completely from the cylinders. This reduces horsepower by not letting the cylinder fill with air and fuel.<P>I've been mulling over a single 3 inch pipe or twin 2½" pipes for my SBM (Small Block Mopar). The 2.8 worked fine with an exhaust I got from IRM; a single 2¼" pipe that split where the muffler should have been, leading to dual twin resonator tips. It sounded sweet. At normal idle, it was a burble reminiscent of Big Blocks, and at speed, it was a respectable roar that made me turn the stereo up. The only thing that *stunk* about this setup is that it didn't take long for the Hooker tips to rust through and eventually fall off on their own....<P>------------------<BR>This should work until my site comes online....   <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.rshuman/files/Tmh.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||88formula||12-03-2000||10:58 PM||||How about one big one like the one on this guys car. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tailpipe2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
