Z||000015||jlhuber||12-03-2000||11:44 PM||||I know about the too low of backpressure deal caused by the pipes being too big, but that only applies if the entire system is too big.  Would an entire system of that diameter even physically fit in a fiero without having to hack up the trunk?  As with most others who have that style of a tip on their car, it is just the tip that is that size, something along the lines of 2.5 inch inlet and 3.5 to 4 inch outlet.  There are no performance benefits of having a tip of that magnitude, it is all for looks.  What is it they say, "all show, no go."  Hey, to each his own.  <P>I would still like to know what is up with that *jet car* that is pictured above.  I have seen it many times and still can't figure it out.||||reg||1
